  "description": "Brings the Rust wgpu and glam crates, and the crate codebrix-webgpu (the WebGPU context, a canvas host with layers and one clock, the maths), to the browser frontend of a CodeBrix.WebPlatform application, for showing 3D graphics, scenes and animations through WebGPU: the third-party crates exactly as crates.io published them, carried with codebrix-webgpu as one archive with their third-party notices, and the one call the build program makes to register them as a crate bundle, so that the frontend builds offline.",
